`]})}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Encoding “other”, rank by rank",children:[e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["Encoding ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"other"})," starts from five symbols, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"[o, t, h, e, r]"}),", and applies the four ranks in order. Rank 1, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"t + h"}),", gives ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"[o, th, e, r]"}),". Rank 2, ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"th + e"}),", gives ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"[o, the, r]"}),". Rank 3 needs ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"the"})," followed by a space, and ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"other"})," has none. Rank 4 needs an ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"e"})," directly before an ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"r"}),", but the ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"e"})," is now part of ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"the"}),"."]}),e.jsxs(t.p,{children:["The order decides the result. Applied with ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"e + r"})," before ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"th + e"}),", the same four merges would give ",e.jsx(t.code,{children:"[o, th, er]"}),"."]})]})]})]}),`
